# Product update workflow (ERP → Shopify)

When changing product data that appears on the storefront (title/name, description, tags, price, inventory, publish status, handles, images, etc.):

1. **Update the local ERP database first** (`products` and related tables).
2. **Then push to Shopify** from the updated ERP row (`ShopifyProductUpsertFromErpService`, bulk push job, or `ShopifyProductPushBySkusService`).

Shopify is a mirror of ERP. Pushing without saving ERP first means the next bulk/department push will **overwrite** Shopify with stale ERP data.

## Default agent behavior

Unless the user explicitly says otherwise (e.g. “Shopify only”, “skip ERP”, “temporary Shopify hotfix”):

- Persist ERP changes before any Shopify write.
- After ERP apply, push affected SKUs to Shopify in the same task when storefront-visible fields changed.
- Report both steps: ERP rows updated + Shopify push result.

## Exceptions (user must be explicit)

- **Shopify-only hotfix** with no ERP change.
- **ERP-only** backfill with no storefront push yet.

## Naming conventions

Prefer canonical title maps + rename commands (see `StediTweezerTitleResolver`, `StediAntiStaticBrushTitleResolver`) over one-off Shopify Admin edits.
